analeptique-by-acetate (1.0+1-0ddebs10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Changes prepared with Claude Opus 5.5
  * debian/control : depend on libsdl1.2debian through ${shlibs:Depends}
    (provided by sdl12-compat); libsdl1.2-compat does not exist on
    resolute, which made the package uninstallable. Removed the useless
    libglu-dev build dependency. Better description
  * Removed the launcher script: the intro is installed as
    /usr/bin/analeptique-by-acetate
  * debian/patches/01_adapt_makefile.patch : use CPPFLAGS (fortify) and
    LDLIBS, no longer link with GLU
  * debian/patches/03_quit_on_window_close.patch : quit when the window
    is closed
  * debian/patches/04_init_variable.patch : initialise a variable read
    before being set
  * debian/resources : added the missing icon (was an empty file)
  * debian/resources/*.desktop : added Keywords, single main category
  * debian/*.lintian-overrides : documented the overrides, removed the
    desktop keywords one, added the pandoc groff-message one
  * debian/*.6 : rewritten, documented the keys
  * debian/docs : removed (empty)

 -- Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:04:51 +0100

